      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C25", "C34", "C03", "C09"]
    },
    {
      "family": "current_gold_voting_records",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C32", "C14", "C19", "C20"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct measured oral bioavailability for the query molecule itself.",
    "Dose and formulation for the query are unspecified; odanacatib shows dose-dependent F (70% at 10 mg vs 30% at 50 mg).",
    "Solubility and dissolution of the query are not directly measured; high logP and low Fsp3 raise a possible absorption limitation.",
    "First-pass metabolism and clearance of the query are not directly assessed."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "The query's 4-methylsulfonylphenyl-containing biaryl scaffold is supported by multiple fasted-state human absolute bioavailability measurements in structurally related drugs (esaxerenone 89%, BI 425809 71.6%, odanacatib 30-70%), all above the 20% threshold. Although the physicochemical prior is mixed and solubility is uncertain, the transferable direct F evidence supports a high prediction."
}

